        "title": "Migrate ClaudeOAuthRefreshFailureGate fingerprint override to a task-local scope",
        "body": "## Summary\nMigrate `ClaudeOAuthRefreshFailureGate`'s fingerprint-provider test override off the unsynchronized\nprocess-global `nonisolated(unsafe) static var fingerprintProviderOverride` onto a task-local scope,\nmirroring `KeychainAccessPreflight`. Part of #2204.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace the static + its `setFingerprintProviderOverrideForTesting` setter with a\n  `FingerprintProviderOverrideStore` (`@unchecked Sendable`), a `@TaskLocal` store, and sync + async\n  `withFingerprintProviderOverrideForTesting` scopes. `currentFingerprint()` now reads the task-local store.\n- The non-macOS stub gains the matching `with…` scopes (loose `(() -> Any?)?` — `AuthFingerprint` is\n  macOS-only, as with the prior setter stub).\n- Move the ~10 test call sites from `set…{ }` / `defer set…(nil)` to the scoped\n  `with…{ provider } operation: { … }` form (unblocks-on-fingerprint-change semantics preserved — the\n  provider closure captures the mutated `var` by reference).\n\n## Validation\n- `make check` → 0 violations / 1465 files.\n- Full suite, contract config (`GROUP_SIZE=4 TIMEOUT=120 RETRY=0`): 660 selections / 165 groups, all\n  pass (one keychain-live-proof group timed out under local concurrent-build load and recovered;\n  re-run isolated = 4 suites pass in 0.79s — unrelated to this diff). Migrated\n  `ClaudeOAuthRefreshFailureGateTests` pass clean in 0.038s.\n- Behavior-neutral: overrides were never written outside `…ForTesting` seams; task-local scoping\n  eliminates the unsynchronized global rather than locking it.\n\n## Related\n- Part of https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/2204 · follows #2239, #2240.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Remaining #2204 seams (`CookieHeaderCache`, `KeychainAccessGate`) — separate PRs. No account/auth-file\n  behavior changes. Screenshots not applicable (non-UI).\n\n## Notes\n- No CHANGELOG entry — internal test synchronization only.\n\nReview history: https://gist.github.com/f635aaeb1ad3b4023e9e4ba20dfa7830\nAuthored with Claude.\n",
